DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  calculate  the  principal value of the arc sine of _x;
       that is the value whose sine is _x.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the principal value of the arc  sine
       of _x in radians; the return value is in the range [-pi/2, pi/2].

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.

       If  _x is outside the range [-1, 1], a domain error occurs, and a NaN is
       returned.

EERRRROORRSS
       See mmaatthh__eerrrroorr(7) for information on how to determine whether an  error
       has occurred when calling these functions.

       The following errors can occur:

       Domain error: _x is outside the range [-1, 1]
              _e_r_r_n_o  is  set  to  EEDDOOMM.   An  invalid floating‐point exception
              (FFEE__IINNVVAALLIIDD) is raised.

